explanation\": \"A crucial aspect of NBR 14535 is its incorporation of TIA 607, the standard that defines requirements for grounding and bonding in structured cabling systems. This integration is vital for ensuring the safety and proper functioning of these systems within Brazil [Data: Relationships (2443)].\\n\\nBy adopting TIA 607's protocols, NBR 14535 provides clear guidelines for grounding practices, which are fundamental to preventing electrical hazards and ensuring the integrity of data transmission. The emphasis on grounding reflects the standard's commitment to robust and safe infrastructure development across all cabling applications it covers [Data: Entities (1547), Relationships (2443)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Future-proofing with TIA 568-5 Integration\",\n      \"explanation\": \"NBR 14535 is designed to evolve, with plans to reference or incorporate specifications from the future standard TIA 568-5 (2022). This forward-looking approach ensures that the Brazilian standard remains current with the latest advancements in cabling technology [Data: Relationships (2454)].\\n\\nBy aligning with upcoming international standards like TIA 568-5, NBR 14535 demonstrates a commitment to maintaining high levels of technical relevance and performance in Brazil's cabling infrastructure. This proactive stance helps industries anticipate and adopt new technologies and methodologies, contributing to a more advanced and resilient national network infrastructure [Data: Entities (1551), Relationships (2454)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Brazilian Context and Coexistence with US Standards\",\n      \"explanation\": \"NBR 14535 is specifically adapted to the national context of Brazil, reflecting local regulations and requirements. This tailoring ensures its practical applicability and relevance for the Brazilian market [Data: Entities (1403), Relationships (2458)].\\n\\nDespite the existence and adoption of NBR 14535, it is noteworthy that US standards continue to be frequently utilized in tenders and projects within Brazil. This indicates a coexistence where international standards are often specified, possibly due to familiarity, existing industry practices, or specific project requirements, alongside the national Brazilian standard [Data: Entities (1403)].\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rating\": 7.5,\n  \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is high due to the foundational nature of cabling infrastructure standards for critical sectors like data centers and healthcare, and their application within a major economy like Brazil.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {"native_finish_reason": "STOP"}}], "created": 1788041254, "model": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": "default", "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1393, "prompt_tokens": 3234, "total_tokens": 4627, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null, "image_tokens": 0}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost": 0.0008806, "is_byok": false, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.0008806, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.0003234, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.0005572}}, "formatted_response": null, "provider": "Google", "content": "{\n  \"title\": \"NBR 14535: Brazilian Cabling Infrastructure Standards\",\n  \"summary\": \"This report details the NBR 14535 standard, a Brazilian framework for cabling infrastructure that adapts and integrates international standards such as TIA 942 (data centers), TIA 1179 (healthcare), and TIA 607 (grounding). It is designed for the Brazilian context but coexists wi